WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Safex

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:09.701
The situation of the war in Europe
is getting worse and worse.

00:00:09.851 --> 00:00:12.103
The Merry Jane Nursing School

00:00:12.253 --> 00:00:16.076
is recruiting a nurse
for the army, under order.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:26.183
Franny volunteers
for this nursing job.

00:00:30.264 --> 00:00:31.657
As a result,

00:00:31.807 --> 00:00:35.790
Franny is heading

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.030
for the European battlefield.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.806
The family that bore love and hatred.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.403
I really wonder how Franny is doing.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:17.540
After she went to the front line
as a nurse,

00:01:18.679 --> 00:01:22.342
I start to get the feeling the war
is close to my life as never before.

00:01:24.051 --> 00:01:25.477
I want to write to her,

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:27.986
but I don't know where she could be.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:33.218
Franny, when we were together,

00:01:33.368 --> 00:01:37.089
there were times
I wanted you to go away.

00:01:37.239 --> 00:01:39.496
Now I'm feeling very lonely.

00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:06.818
Good morning, everyone!

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:08.086
Morning!

00:02:08.236 --> 00:02:11.096
What happened
to the cold-hearted four-eye frog?

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.625
Cold-hearted four-eye frog?
That's very rude.

00:02:13.775 --> 00:02:16.061
Because she's as cold as ice.

00:02:16.211 --> 00:02:18.400
Cold-hearted four-eye frog.
She deserves that!

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.036
Franny went to the front line
voluntarily, as an army nurse.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.106
We should be nicer to her.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:31.606
Let's pray for Franny.

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:54.565
Franny will be an army nurse.

00:02:54.715 --> 00:02:56.802
She didn't tell her parents at all.

00:02:56.952 --> 00:02:58.436
Are you kidding?

00:02:58.586 --> 00:03:02.375
Even though I go to the battlefield,
my family wouldn't worry about me.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:07.642
My father gets drunk everyday
and quarrels with my mom.

00:03:08.255 --> 00:03:11.224
My brother and sister
never give a helping hand to others.

00:03:11.825 --> 00:03:14.089
Everybody lives their own lives.

00:03:14.828 --> 00:03:18.256
You think a family like that
would care anything about me?

00:03:18.406 --> 00:03:19.798
Don't be silly.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:23.428
And don't worry about me either.

00:03:23.678 --> 00:03:25.161
But Franny...

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.966
Franny,

00:03:28.116 --> 00:03:31.499
even if we're not your family,
we do worry about you.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:36.914
The patients pray for your safety.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.377
Maybe it's not my business,

00:03:39.527 --> 00:03:41.886
but I need to tell your family.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.781
I have a day off tomorrow.

00:03:43.931 --> 00:03:47.385
But I have no idea where Franny lives.

00:03:47.535 --> 00:03:48.987
We've been close for a long time,

00:03:49.137 --> 00:03:51.758
but I hardly even know her address.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:56.427
Franny Hamilton.

00:03:56.577 --> 00:03:57.931
I got it!

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:00.832
Thank you!

00:04:00.982 --> 00:04:03.774
Wester Street No. 360, Chicago City.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.077
Franny's home is
a little bit far from here,

00:04:13.227 --> 00:04:15.211
but I think I could be back
before evening.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:25.794
Oh, no! There's no carriage !

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.960
Candy!

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:29.729
Stear!

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.629
Are you on your day off?

00:04:31.779 --> 00:04:32.697
Yes.

00:04:32.847 --> 00:04:36.167
Why didn't you tell me, Candy?

00:04:36.517 --> 00:04:37.835
I am quite busy today.

00:04:37.985 --> 00:04:40.205
I am going to visit Franny's family.

00:04:40.555 --> 00:04:43.942
You're going to Franny's house?
I can give you a ride.

00:04:44.292 --> 00:04:45.777
- But....
- Is that inconvenient?

00:04:45.927 --> 00:04:47.011
I don't want to bother you.

00:04:47.361 --> 00:04:50.948
Not at all. Archie and Annie
are going out for a date.

00:04:51.098 --> 00:04:54.952
I have nothing to do,
so I'm hanging out on the streets.

00:04:55.102 --> 00:04:56.585
I see.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.956
Today I can drive you anywhere you like.

00:04:59.106 --> 00:05:00.725
Hop on!

00:05:00.875 --> 00:05:02.233
Thank you, Stear.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.729
It's my honour to offer you a ride.

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.433
Let's go!

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:15.746
Franny's decision to be an army nurse
is very respectable.

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:20.115
But I still don't think she should
hide this decision from her parents.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.546
You're going to tell her family?

00:05:21.696 --> 00:05:23.446
It's not my business?

00:05:23.596 --> 00:05:25.252
No. You're doing the right thing.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:27.388
I feel more relieved, thank you.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.037
Stear, the car is on fire!

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:54.646
That's ok. It's only overheated.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:56.945
Let's get some water from there.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:05.389
It's hot!

00:06:05.539 --> 00:06:07.364
Candy, hand me some water.

00:06:09.101 --> 00:06:11.069
The water is in the back.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:17.785
Done!

00:06:17.935 --> 00:06:19.775
Stear, has Patty ever written to you?

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:21.436
Yes, just a couple weeks ago.

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:23.608
Is everything ok with her?

00:06:23.998 --> 00:06:26.311
She says hi to you.

00:06:26.619 --> 00:06:29.747
She didn't write me a word.

00:06:30.097 --> 00:06:31.749
She told me in the letter that

00:06:31.899 --> 00:06:35.385
she really wants to meet you
and have a chat about old times.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:39.237
Our ears would be overused
and callused next time we meet.

00:06:39.507 --> 00:06:40.865
That's possible.

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:44.000
I wish she could come to the States.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.405
Serve in the army voluntarily.

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:54.175
Our country needs
volunteer soldiers for the war.

00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:00.845
There will be more people
going to the battlefields.

00:07:00.995 --> 00:07:03.388
The war would be
more and more intense.

00:07:21.106 --> 00:07:22.471
Let's go.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.827
My face is all covered with dust.

00:07:33.977 --> 00:07:36.632
I want to find a place to wash my face.

00:07:36.805 --> 00:07:37.999
OK.

00:07:51.253 --> 00:07:53.346
It's so beautiful here!

00:07:53.522 --> 00:07:56.919
Before the war,
Europe was as beautiful as here.

00:07:57.559 --> 00:07:59.720
Here's Franny's hometown.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:02.623
If Franny had a boyfriend now,
do you think she'd still go?

00:08:03.398 --> 00:08:06.367
Franny would definitely go.
That's how she is.

00:08:07.202 --> 00:08:11.366
She values the mission
of nursing the most.

00:08:37.366 --> 00:08:39.300
Stop!
I'm going to ask for directions.

00:08:42.604 --> 00:08:44.197
Excuse me,
how can I get to this address?

00:08:44.347 --> 00:08:45.967
What address?

00:08:49.111 --> 00:08:54.107
Franny Hamilton! She's the daughter
of Hamilton, the drunk.

00:08:54.257 --> 00:08:55.442
I know him.

00:08:55.592 --> 00:08:57.344
Hamilton the drunk?

00:08:57.494 --> 00:09:00.518
Yes. Just go straight along this street.

00:09:03.392 --> 00:09:05.223
Drive a little further.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.061
It's that house over there.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.511
Here we are.

00:09:28.216 --> 00:09:30.707
It's weird!

00:09:31.352 --> 00:09:34.913
Excuse me, is anybody home?

00:09:39.194 --> 00:09:42.908
Hi, I'm Candy, a friend of Franny.

00:09:54.642 --> 00:09:56.407
Can I come in?

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:00.743
Nobody's home?

00:10:01.683 --> 00:10:04.010
I want to meet your parents.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.950
Where are they?

00:10:30.945 --> 00:10:33.273
Brother, you have to come back today!

00:10:33.723 --> 00:10:36.044
Idiot! I won't!

00:10:37.418 --> 00:10:38.749
You little street gangster!

00:10:46.261 --> 00:10:47.626
Are they there?

00:10:51.199 --> 00:10:54.293
Get out of here, you drunk!

00:10:59.707 --> 00:11:03.074
You're such an annoying old woman!

00:11:04.712 --> 00:11:07.281
Annoying old woman!

00:11:12.053 --> 00:11:13.782
Is he your father?

00:11:19.627 --> 00:11:22.555
Mr. Hamilton, are you alright?
Put yourself together!

00:11:22.805 --> 00:11:24.757
That's ok. He's always like that.

00:11:25.107 --> 00:11:27.794
But we can't let him lie down
on the street.

00:11:27.944 --> 00:11:29.529
Help me, Stear.

00:11:29.679 --> 00:11:30.696
Sure.

00:11:31.773 --> 00:11:33.035
Come on.

00:11:33.674 --> 00:11:36.272
I don't know who you are.
Please mind your own business.

00:11:36.978 --> 00:11:38.638
But....

00:11:38.788 --> 00:11:41.876
It's ok. He's my husband.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.978
You're Franny's mom?

00:11:45.428 --> 00:11:47.980
Old woman, listen up!

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:53.049
Nobody can bully me if I ain't here!

00:12:23.724 --> 00:12:25.685
Excuse me, are you Franny's mother?

00:12:25.835 --> 00:12:28.126
Franny? Who are you?

00:12:29.096 --> 00:12:32.458
I am Franny's friend, Candice White.

00:12:32.608 --> 00:12:34.527
I am Candy's friend. My name is Stear.

00:12:34.677 --> 00:12:37.397
Did Franny ask you to come?

00:12:37.947 --> 00:12:38.951
No.

00:12:39.181 --> 00:12:42.837
If you are looking for Franny,
I know nothing about her.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:44.937
She left this home without
saying goodbye, to become a nurse.

00:12:45.087 --> 00:12:46.973
I've got no message from her since then.

00:12:47.223 --> 00:12:49.612
Franny left without saying goodbye?

00:12:50.384 --> 00:12:52.375
She's always being selfish,

00:12:55.323 --> 00:12:58.554
without any consideration of my pain.

00:12:58.859 --> 00:13:02.888
Please don't worry about her.
Franny is an outstanding nurse.

00:13:03.038 --> 00:13:04.657
What kind of outstanding nurse?

00:13:04.807 --> 00:13:08.094
She abandoned her parents
and left her family behind.

00:13:08.244 --> 00:13:11.263
She's not qualified to be a nurse at all!

00:13:13.707 --> 00:13:15.334
This is Mr. Hamilton's saloon?

00:13:15.784 --> 00:13:17.199
Yes.

00:13:18.679 --> 00:13:19.705
You have a package.

00:13:20.155 --> 00:13:21.509
A package?

00:13:23.517 --> 00:13:25.077
Thank you.

00:13:25.227 --> 00:13:27.613
Who sent it? It's from Franny!

00:13:27.763 --> 00:13:29.049
Franny?

00:13:34.128 --> 00:13:37.689
Dear mom, I became a real nurse,
as I always dreamed of.

00:13:38.265 --> 00:13:41.098
Now I'll continue my nursing work
in Europe.

00:13:42.235 --> 00:13:44.495
The pipe is for dad,
the hair pin is for mom,

00:13:44.672 --> 00:13:48.301
the harmonica is for my brother,
and the candies are for my sister.

00:13:51.845 --> 00:13:56.008
All my money is saved
in this piggy bank,

00:13:56.158 --> 00:13:58.517
and I hope these things
will be of help to you. Franny.

00:13:59.486 --> 00:14:01.113
There isn't much money.

00:14:01.263 --> 00:14:04.583
Do you think this little money
is enough to pay us back?

00:14:04.733 --> 00:14:06.285
Silly girl!

00:14:06.735 --> 00:14:08.590
No, Franny is really respectable.

00:14:09.096 --> 00:14:10.522
Respectable for what?

00:14:10.972 --> 00:14:12.925
She didn't mention in the letter,

00:14:13.275 --> 00:14:16.195
but in fact she stands out
for the victims on the front line.

00:14:16.345 --> 00:14:19.965
She goes to the European battlefields.
She'll be an army nurse.

00:14:20.115 --> 00:14:22.000
Franny is going to be an army nurse?!

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:24.036
Why didn't she get back
and discuss it with us?

00:14:24.186 --> 00:14:25.938
She's trying to let me worry
on purpose.

00:14:26.088 --> 00:14:27.573
She is afraid of worrying you,

00:14:27.723 --> 00:14:29.441
that's why she didn't send
any word to you.

00:14:29.591 --> 00:14:31.777
She sent you all her savings,

00:14:31.927 --> 00:14:35.083
because she has already
made up her mind.

00:14:35.255 --> 00:14:37.849
She's going to the front line voluntarily.

00:14:38.592 --> 00:14:40.150
Such a silly girl!

00:14:42.596 --> 00:14:43.927
She shouldn't have done that.

00:14:44.331 --> 00:14:46.925
It's no difference between victims
and patients from different nations.

00:14:47.075 --> 00:14:49.798
We, as nurses,
can't discriminate anyone.

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:53.665
Nationality and race don't matter.

00:14:53.815 --> 00:14:55.312
Everyone is equal.

00:14:55.462 --> 00:14:58.605
Franny knows it well.

00:14:58.845 --> 00:15:01.807
Maybe she hates her family.

00:15:01.957 --> 00:15:04.312
No, she wishes
she could hate her family,

00:15:04.751 --> 00:15:08.280
but she just couldn't
leave you behind in the end.

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:11.416
She's eager to meet you all.

00:15:11.866 --> 00:15:14.688
That's why she sent this package
after all.

00:15:18.598 --> 00:15:20.092
Luckily, I came here.

00:15:20.242 --> 00:15:22.160
I finally understand
the difficulties that Franny faces.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.169
It makes me admire her
and feel sorry for her.

00:15:28.775 --> 00:15:30.766
Get out!

00:15:31.177 --> 00:15:33.571
Get out now!

00:15:42.489 --> 00:15:47.552
Our family is without any merits,
we don't need any lustre and glory.

00:15:48.461 --> 00:15:50.088
Angel in white.

00:15:52.966 --> 00:15:54.399
Hilarious!

00:16:08.114 --> 00:16:10.508
The hair pin is for mom,
the pipe is for dad,

00:16:10.658 --> 00:16:13.844
the harmonica is for my brother,
and the candies are for my sister.

00:16:19.091 --> 00:16:20.222
Franny!

00:16:45.251 --> 00:16:46.775
Good bye.

00:17:20.152 --> 00:17:21.380
Here you are, Candy.

00:17:22.321 --> 00:17:23.915
Thank you for today, Stear.

00:17:24.065 --> 00:17:26.884
No, I want to say thank you, too.
I understood a lot of things today.

00:17:27.034 --> 00:17:30.134
Franny's family will change
her mind eventually.

00:17:30.284 --> 00:17:32.123
They definitely will.

00:17:32.273 --> 00:17:33.460
Good bye, Stear.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.293
Good bye, Candy.

00:17:35.443 --> 00:17:37.233
Bye.

00:17:51.784 --> 00:17:55.245
What happened in the hospital?
It's noisy.

00:17:56.022 --> 00:17:57.281
What happened?

00:17:57.531 --> 00:18:01.051
That guy is frightening.
He hasn't been identified yet.

00:18:01.861 --> 00:18:02.864
What's wrong?

00:18:03.104 --> 00:18:05.356
Candy, he seems to be a spy.

00:18:05.506 --> 00:18:06.724
A spy?

00:18:06.874 --> 00:18:10.594
We're not sure.
We heard that he's a prisoner.

00:18:10.744 --> 00:18:12.363
I don't like that.

00:18:12.513 --> 00:18:16.100
And he was sent to our hospital
from the European battlefields.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:17.868
From the battlefields?

00:18:18.018 --> 00:18:19.438
Make way!

00:18:21.313 --> 00:18:22.810
Make way, nurses!

00:18:24.817 --> 00:18:26.114
He's that guy.

00:18:28.987 --> 00:18:31.321
He looks like he's lost all his energy
and is as white as a sheet.

00:18:36.629 --> 00:18:39.223
His mouth looks familiar.

00:18:39.373 --> 00:18:41.664
Is it really possible that he is...

00:18:42.468 --> 00:18:43.935
A skunk!

00:18:46.572 --> 00:18:50.406
- Is that a skunk?
- It's stinky!

00:18:50.876 --> 00:18:52.434
Get out!

00:18:54.613 --> 00:18:56.307
Isn't that Poope?

00:18:56.457 --> 00:18:57.457
Poope!

00:19:01.153 --> 00:19:04.783
Poope, it's really you!

00:19:13.165 --> 00:19:16.093
Poope, that guy...

00:19:17.536 --> 00:19:20.431
His name is Poope.
He wants to be friends with you.

00:19:20.881 --> 00:19:22.838
My name's Candy. Nice to meet you!

00:19:24.843 --> 00:19:28.108
Mr. Albert is always encouraging me.

00:19:36.422 --> 00:19:38.982
Good morning, Candy.

00:19:45.998 --> 00:19:47.727
Mr. Albert!

00:19:48.334 --> 00:19:51.428
I got the letter. Let's get inside.

00:20:00.279 --> 00:20:01.905
This place is really desolate!

00:20:02.405 --> 00:20:03.557
Wait a second.

00:20:03.707 --> 00:20:06.760
You have to pass a test
before you get in.

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:08.268
A test?

00:20:08.537 --> 00:20:09.970
You'll see.

00:20:11.273 --> 00:20:12.472
We have guests!

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:20.671
There are so many of them!

00:20:21.016 --> 00:20:23.610
Kurin, they are all your friends.

00:20:24.119 --> 00:20:25.450
It tickles!

00:20:27.289 --> 00:20:28.388
They're so cute!

00:20:30.726 --> 00:20:32.185
Long time no see, Candy!

00:20:32.335 --> 00:20:34.956
It's really you, Mr. Albert!

00:20:36.631 --> 00:20:37.958
Before I came to London,

00:20:38.108 --> 00:20:40.558
I was really afraid
that I won't see you again.

00:20:41.136 --> 00:20:42.597
Don't cry, Candy.

00:20:42.838 --> 00:20:44.601
Let me take a closer look of you.

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:47.301
You're getting prettier.

00:20:47.476 --> 00:20:49.376
You too, Mr. Albert!

00:20:49.878 --> 00:20:51.436
Mr. Albert...

00:20:51.813 --> 00:20:54.043
Why did he come back
from the European battlefields?

00:20:56.918 --> 00:20:58.916
Candy can't believe it's true.

00:20:59.588 --> 00:21:03.183
That's impossible!

00:21:04.359 --> 00:21:09.256
Candy repeats this sentence
in her heart again and again.
